{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>The Elohim of old.</b> The Prime Cause, and all besides Him is brought into existence anew from Him." "<b>And from beneath, arms of eternity.</b> And below the heavens, He is the Elohim of arms — that is, the guides of the cosmic existents, namely the generated and perishable things that fall under time, such as the qualities of the elements and the nature that feeds, grows, brings forth, and depicts forms in plants and in living beings." "<b>And He drove the enemy from before you, and said: Destroy.</b> He has driven from before you the enemy who was the inhabitant of the land, and He said to you: 'Destroy!' — for not by your sword did you take possession of the land, in such wise that you might suppose that with the decline of your strength over the passage of time, or with the arrival of a successor, the enemies would prevail; for in truth it was He who drove them out, and how could they advance against His will?"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:23:43.535186637Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}